\TL\ has grown over the years from a \DVD\ distributed once a year to a
full-fledged network-enabled system with daily updates. Development of
\TL\ is done in the Subversion repository on \url{tug.org}, and
coordinated on several mailing
lists (\url{https://lists.tug.org}). The network
distribution of \TL\ is served by \acro{CTAN} and their mirror system,
relieving us from serving huge amounts of data to the world, or
reimplementing another mirror system. (Thanks much to \acro{CTAN}.)

Around the main distribution of \TL, several additional services have
accumulated over the years\Dash and in particular in recent months\Dash
so that we thought it a good idea to summarize and present all the
available services in this article. Details about each follow the
overview.
